    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8-a1">

                <pb facs="0106" n="10" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg10"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Long to commandant Navy-Yard, Norfolk, Va</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-06-26"><hi rendition="#italic">June 26,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Argentine school ship, at present
                    cruising in North American waters, will probably visit Hampton Roads in the near
                    future.</p>
                <p>The Department desires you to extend every courtesy that may be practicable to
                    this vessel. And in the event that it is desired for her officers and cadets to
                    visit the <pb facs="0107" n="11" xml:id="pg11"/> works of the Newport News Ship
                    Building and Dry Dock Company and the navy-yard, the Department wishes you to
                    arrange for such visits, and facilitate them so far as may be in your power.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John D. Long</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
